{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlitejournal", "label": "SqliteJournal", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "The right default for single-node production: bun:sqlite is built in on Bun, better-sqlite3 is a single optional peer on Node, node:sqlite covers Deno.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlitesnapshotstore", "label": "SqliteSnapshotStore", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlitedurablestatestore", "label": "SqliteDurableStateStore", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "A remote URL is rejected at construction and points at LibSqlDurableStateStore, because the local driver cannot open one and silently creating a FILE with that name is the confusing outcome.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_busytimeoutms", "label": "busyTimeoutMs", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Set explicitly because the drivers disagree (0 ms on bun:sqlite and node:sqlite, 5000 ms on better-sqlite3), which would make the same journal behave differently per runtime. The default is 1000 ms rather than 5000 because the SQLite drivers are synchronous \u2014 the wait blocks the event loop, cluster heartbeats included \u2014 and the failure detector calls a node unreachable after 2000 ms. A negative value is rejected: SQLite reads it as retry-forever, an unbounded freeze.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_wal_mode", "label": "WAL mode", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Recommended for production \u2014 readers do not block the writer, commits are sequential, crash recovery is simpler. Default off to match SQLite's own defaults.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_driver_auto_detection", "label": "SQLite driver auto-detection", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Bun to bun:sqlite, Node to better-sqlite3 when installed else node:sqlite, Deno to node:sqlite \u2014 every supported runtime has a driver that needs no install. The concrete driver classes are not public API; the driver slot is an internal seam the framework's own tests use.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_dual_table_tag_design", "label": "Dual-table tag design", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "events.tags keeps the legacy CSV column for back-compat while tag queries read the indexed events_tags table instead of scanning every row. Both are written in the same transaction, so they cannot drift apart.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_begin_immediate_concurrency_check", "label": "BEGIN IMMEDIATE head re-read", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Locally the journal re-reads the head sequence inside a BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction and raises JournalConcurrencyError before attempting any insert \u2014 the primary key is only a backstop here. The HTTP-fronted backends have no such transaction and must let the write hit (persistence_id, sequence_nr) instead: same tables, weaker guarantee.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlite_dialect_schema", "label": "SQLite dialect schema", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Five tables (events, events_tags, events_meta, snapshots, durable_state) created with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS, shared verbatim with libSQL/Turso and Cloudflare D1 \u2014 the same DDL runs on all three, which is what lets a database move between them without a migration.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_do_not_share_file_across_processes", "label": "Do not share a SQLite file across processes", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "SQLite supports concurrent processes, but the framework's prepared statements and in-process JournalEventBus do not know about another process's writes, so push-based queries miss cross-process events. Network filesystems break locking outright.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlitejournal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_overview_journal", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlitesnapshotstore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_overview_snapshotstore", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlitedurablestatestore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_overview_durablestatestore", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlite_dialect_schema", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_libsql_libsqljournal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlite_dialect_schema", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_cloudflare_d1_d1journal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlitedurablestatestore", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_libsql_libsqldurablestatestore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/journals/sqlite.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_busytimeoutms", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_journals_sqlite_sqlitejournal", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", 